Aerie-Purpose: Peek an auto-hidden Aerie sidebar open for F6 and for Ctrl+L, from the commands themselves and not from listing the panes.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (browser_view.cc, vertical_tab_strip_region_view.*)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #184. Patch 0032 lets F6 visit the sidebar's panes, and a hidden sidebar adds none. With auto-hide the sidebar is hidden at rest, so
BrowserView::RotatePaneFocusFromView (the F6 rotation) and BrowserView::SetFocusToLocationBar (Ctrl+L, when the user asked for it) now ask the
region view to peek it open first (VerticalTabStripRegionView::PeekAerieSidebarForPaneFocus, which does nothing unless the sidebar is
auto-hidden). Listing the panes (GetAccessiblePanes) is a query again and changes nothing.

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
@@ -3038,6 +3038,12 @@
     return;
   }
 #endif
+  // Aerie (issue #184): Ctrl+L on an auto-hidden sidebar peeks it open, so
+  // that the address pill the omnibox sits in is on screen. Not for a focus the
+  // browser moves itself (a new window or tab).
+  if (is_user_initiated && vertical_tab_strip_region_view_) {
+    vertical_tab_strip_region_view_->PeekAerieSidebarForPaneFocus();
+  }
   if (!IsLocationBarVisible()) {
     return;
   }
@@ -5286,6 +5292,12 @@
 bool BrowserView::RotatePaneFocusFromView(views::View* focused_view,
                                           bool forward,
                                           bool enable_wrapping) {
+  // Aerie (issue #184): F6 on an auto-hidden sidebar peeks it open before the
+  // panes are listed, so that its panes are in the rotation. Listing the panes
+  // changes nothing.
+  if (vertical_tab_strip_region_view_) {
+    vertical_tab_strip_region_view_->PeekAerieSidebarForPaneFocus();
+  }
